.TH SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_MODE_SCALING 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_MODE_SCALING \- A variable controlling how modes with a non-native aspect ratio are displayed under Wayland.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_MODE_SCALING \(dqSDL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_MODE_SCALING\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
When this hint is set, the requested scaling will be used when displaying fullscreen video modes that don\(aqt match the display\(aqs native aspect ratio\[char46] This is contingent on compositor viewport support\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dqaspect\(dq - Video modes will be displayed scaled, in their proper aspect ratio, with black bars\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dqstretch\(dq - Video modes will be scaled to fill the entire display\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqnone\(dq - Video modes will be displayed as 1:1 with no scaling\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before creating a window\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

